{"kind":"report","text":"Re-review of the corrected Tailapp runtime metrics head, exact commit 0e3df616530546eb160ad5a1758847b323a5f2ba (primary artifact 2b0e64de, internal/metrics/metrics.go). Verdict: approved. This fulfills the re-review promise on request #360; I took it over after the prior checker instance stopped mid-promise, re-verified independently in a clean checkout at the exact head, and confirm all three required corrections from changes-requested verdict 2ecc776a are resolved.\n\nGATES (independently rerun at 0e3df616): go test ./... passes (all packages incl. internal/metrics); go vet ./... clean; go test -race ./... on internal/metrics, engine, projection, query, and inbox passes; ./scripts/demo.sh passes (\"three OTLP signals, one-shot installs, cross-harness guard and cost analytics, joined exports, runtime metrics, CLI, and MCP\").\n\nREQUIRED 1 (histogram snapshot invariants under concurrency) — RESOLVED. The separate `count` atomic is removed from the histogram struct; observe() no longer increments an independent counter; snapshot() now derives Count from the same cumulative +Inf bucket it returns (Histogram.Count = cumulative). Count == the terminal +Inf cumulative bucket by construction, so the prior race where Count could exceed the terminal bucket is eliminated structurally, not merely narrowed. TestHistogramSnapshotInvariantsUnderConcurrentObservation exercises concurrent observation and passed under -race; TestHistogramDoesNotTruncateAcrossBucketBoundary covers boundary correctness. Cumulative monotonicity holds because buckets are summed in ascending order.\n\nREQUIRED 2 (expose clock regressions) — RESOLVED. Snapshot gains clock_regressions_total, backed by Registry.clockRegressions and ObserveClockRegression(); engine.go now calls ObserveClockRegression() at the wall-elapsed clamp site (elapsed \u003c 0) for queue-delay/oldest-age, so a clock jump is counted rather than silently clamped. TestWallElapsedCountsClockRegression asserts the counter reaches 1 on a regression.\n\nREQUIRED 3 (restore bounded diagnostic loss dimensions) — RESOLVED. Unrouted intake is now split by fixed signal: ObserveRouting takes a recordsBySignal map and increments intake.unroutedSignal over the closed {log,span,metric,unknown} set, surfaced as unrouted_records_by_signal (TestUnroutedIntakeIsSplitBySignal confirms both the total and the per-signal split). Detached obligations are now attributed by a fixed close reason — detachedReason maps to the closed enum {projection_gap, runtime_upgrade, tailapp_deleted, other} — both globally (intake.detachedReason -\u003e detached_obligations_by_reason) and per active Tailapp (Processing.detached -\u003e processing[app].detached_obligations_total), wired at all three detach sites (projection_gap, runtime_upgrade, tailapp_deleted). The per-Tailapp series is bounded: handles are created on activation and removed by delete(e.processing, name) in Engine.Delete, so cardinality tracks currently active/installed definitions with a removal lifecycle, exactly as the accepted design requires. Reasons and signals are fixed enums, never raw input.\n\nADVISORY items from 2ecc776a — cancellation classification is RESOLVED: queryOutcome now returns a distinct \"cancelled\" outcome (registered in the query outcome set), verified by TestQueryMetricOutcomeDistinguishesCancellation. The remaining advisories (sub-millisecond buckets, processing-outcome taxonomy) are acceptable as-is for v1.\n\nONE STANDING ADVISORY, non-blocking: cumulative uint64 counters (records_total, canonical_bytes_total, obligations, per-signal/per-reason maps, histogram bucket counts) are still emitted as raw JSON numbers rather than the decimal-string or explicitly-capped form the metrics-contract advice (report 61f05b05, Required 1) recommended. At sustained high volume a canonical_bytes or records counter can cross the JSON exact-integer limit (2^53) and lose precision for a strict consumer. This does not block approval — it is a forward-looking hardening the design advice already flagged — but adopt decimal-string encoding for the cumulative uint64 fields before a high-throughput production deployment, and add a bump to SnapshotVersion when you do.\n\nEXACT-HEAD ARTIFACTS CITED (all 23 at 0e3df616530546eb160ad5a1758847b323a5f2ba): README.md; docs/README.md; docs/reference/cli.md; docs/reference/mcp.md; docs/reference/metrics.md; internal/cli/cli.go; internal/cli/cli_test.go; internal/control/control.go; internal/control/control_test.go; internal/engine/engine.go; internal/engine/engine_test.go; internal/inbox/inbox.go; internal/inbox/inbox_test.go; internal/ingest/receiver.go; internal/ingest/receiver_test.go; internal/mcp/server.go; internal/mcp/server_test.go; internal/metrics/metrics.go; internal/metrics/metrics_test.go; internal/projection/projection.go; internal/query/query.go; internal/query/query_test.go; scripts/demo.sh.\n\nApproved at exact head 0e3df616530546eb160ad5a1758847b323a5f2ba. The bounded self-observability contract is now implemented with correct concurrent histogram invariants, visible clock-regression accounting, and the fixed-dimension loss measures (unrouted-by-signal, detached-by-reason, per-active-Tailapp) that let an operator distinguish healthy intake from no-consumer, data loss, and backlog."}